message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Composite-gravity black hole PRL verification package"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/quantum-like/composite-gravity-bh-prl"
repository-code: "https://github.com/quantum-like/composite-gravity-bh-prl"
abstract: >-
  Symbolic checks and figure assets for the Physical Review Letters
  submission on the static composite-gravity black hole (draft title in
  the scripts: "Gauge-regular but metric-singular"). This repository is
  the data and code availability package for that submission. It ships
  the verification programs as provided and the merged invariant figure.
  It does not re-derive the theory. Conventions stated in the scripts
  follow Öttinger, J. Phys. Commun. 10, 105003 (2026): tetrad (45),
  metric (46), solution (51), composition rule (4), field strength (18),
  and field equations (19). Units in both scripts are r0 = 1
  (geometrized, r0 = Gm/c^2). The scripts check (49) versus (19), the
  Lie-algebra invariant F·F, and curvature-related metric invariants
  (PPN β = γ = 1, the photon sphere, and Killing surface gravity).
authors:
